  "qualified": [
    "All eight fixture values round-trip under CBOR, raw Postcard and bounded Postcard.",
    "Every truncated prefix and one trailing byte reject for every fixture and codec.",
    "Bounded codec rejects exhausted byte/allocation/node/depth allowances and a short input declaring one million zero-width elements.",
    "Invalid bool and trailing-data failures are asserted as typed ic_wire errors.",
    "PocketIC persists the bounded funding record in stable memory; an update overwrites it and traps; subsequent calls recover the exact original record and repeat reads are unchanged.",
    "Both final managed Root artifacts pass existing Wasm admission guards."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Microbenchmarks are not end-to-end workload latency or cycle-cost estimates.",
    "Auth session bytes are opaque 2KiB fixture contents, not a production login validation.",
    "Selected storage record excerpts are tested, not every maintained record schema.",
    "Stable-write rollback proof is not full Root funding/custody recovery acceptance.",
    "Bounded funding encoding is slower than CBOR; maximum u128 values grow and are slower.",
    "The scratch prototype is not a release-qualified implementation. No broad suite, staging, commit, version change, release or deployment was run."
  ],
  "before_production_cut": [
    "Inventory record-specific byte/allocation/node/depth allowances, including unbounded Storable paths and large checkpoints.",
    "Separate canonical authority/checkpoint/receipt hash encoders from persistence while preserving their accepted bytes.",
    "Update storage schema identities, footprints and exact-byte/current malformed-input tests with their owners.",
    "Qualify actual same-release interruption, paid-effect replay, checkpoint and restoration paths on regenerated installed artifacts."
  ],
